  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "A student visa is a key to study abroad. To be a student in a degree program or a language course, it is necessary to obtain a student visa from the host country you are planning to study in. All documents must be submitted in due time to apply for a student visa. However, the requested documents may vary depending on the chosen countries.\n\nStudents are generally requested to submit the following documents for the student visa applications:\n\nStudents coming from non-EU countries who wish to study in European Union must obtain a residence permit. Non-EU citizens need to apply for a student residence permit to stay longer than 90 days in the EU. The duration of the residence permit cannot exceed the entire period of study. Permits may be subjected to renewal depending on the length of stay and specific regulations in each country.\n\nPeople aiming to study in Ireland need to apply for a D Type Visa, which is for long stays, and all international students studying in Ireland must apply for a residence permit.\n\nStudents need to submit relevant documents to prove the purpose of their stay. For example:"
    ]
